<title>GERMANY: Star Alliance sees 5 to 6 pct growth in passengers.</title>
<headline>Star Alliance sees 5 to 6 pct growth in passengers.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Star Alliance, the newly-announced airline partnership, said on Wednesday it expected annual global passenger growth among partner airlines of five to six percent.</p>
<p>The alliance, formally named on Wednesday at a news conference, currently includes Deutsche Lufthansa AG, United Airlines, SAS, Air Canada, Thai International Airways Ltd and Varig.</p>
<p>A Lufthansa official also said annual cargo shipments would grow six to seven percent among the partner airlines.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
